ampbell, adapted from an off-Broadway stage musical, “X: The Musical” that had first opened in Los Angeles in 1998. Its songs included numbers with titles like 'Listen to Jesus, Jimmy', 'The Stuff', and 'Little Mary Sunshine'. The source material for the musical was a low-budget 1936 American black-and-white film, originally financed by a small church group and released by them under the earnest title 'Tell Your Children'. The film was swiftly purchased by an exploitation producer named Dwain Esper, who re-edited it with added salacious content before re-releasing it under a different name, X. It had almost entirely fallen out of circulation by the 1950s, and survived at all only because its copyright was never properly renewed, leaving it in the public domain. In 1972, founder of an American advocacy organization, purchased a print of the film from the Library of Congress for 297 dollars and began screening it on college campuses, where audiences laughed uproariously at material that had once been presented as grave moral instruction. ID X, probably the first stoner movie ever. ‎", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-20T18:20:32Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "reefer madness?", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-20T18:20:37Z", "username": "Khandoba", "text": "Shubhankar sent this earlier but my god vats doesn’t give a lot of openings", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-20T18:20:39Z", "username": "Srijan Naayak", "text": "Kaafi short question hai, ye quiz khatam hone tak to padh hi lunga ‎", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": true, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-20T18:20:57Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "Reefer Madness is correct!", "role": "confirmation", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]